values ('b3c4d5e6-7f8a-4c03-8d23-4e5f6a7b8c33', 'urban-sociology', 'Urban Sociology', 'Urban sociology provides a comprehensive examination of cities as social laboratories where inequality, culture, and infrastructure intersect. This course balances foundational theory with contemporary issues such as spatial inequality, urban governance, climate resilience, and planetary urbanization. Students will engage with spatial methods, policy analysis, and comparative global urbanism to understand the complex forces shaping modern metropolitan life.');

